 "notes": [
  "Strong's H5090 covers two senses OSHB's own morphology tags distinguish by letter: \"5090 a\" (drive/lead/carry away -- attested in both Qal and Piel) and \"5090 b\" (a single Piel participle, מְנַהֲגוֹת, Nah.2.8, \"moan\", of doves). Since both share one Strong's number they can't be split into separate root entries (would violate the one-Strong's-number-per-file rule), so this file's Piel stem ships only the letter-b \"moan\" form. Piel also has extensive letter-a \"drive/lead\" attestations (e.g. Deut.4.27, Exod.10.13) not included here since they'd conflict with the \"moan\" gloss on this same stem slot -- flagged in case a \"drive/lead\" Piel sense is wanted added separately."
